```javascript
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(details => {
  if (details.reason === 'install') {
    // Inject the JavaScript code into all open tabs
    chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, tabs => {
      tabs.forEach(tab => {
        injectScript(tab.id);
      });
    });
  }
});
```
3. Create a function (e.g., `injectScript`) to inject the JavaScript code into a specific tab. Add the following code to the `background.js` script:
```javascript
function injectScript(tabId) {
  chrome.tabs.executeScript(tabId, {
    file: 'your_javascript_file.js'
  });
}
```
Replace `'your_javascript_file.js'` with the path to your JavaScript file that contains the code you want to inject into the webpage.
4. Create a manifest file (e.g., `manifest.json`) for your extension. This file will describe your extension's properties and permissions.
